{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790615175,"nonce":"Ey11Yym3OzpD3IlGRGm2A4BJSFo=","title":"git work migrate imports any git-bug repository","message":"Decided 2026-09-28 (Luis): a migrate from git-bug is worth having, at very low priority, and entities/bug stays for it rather than leaving in the deletion round (860d6e0).\n\nToday `git work migrate` is this tracker's one-time migration (bf6f392), not an import path for anyone else:\n- it reads refs/issues/*, our renamed namespace (be69e67, bug.Namespace = \"issues\"), where upstream git-bug writes refs/bugs/*;\n- it maps our own labels (area:*, phase:*, ...) onto fields with a hardcoded table and refuses any label it cannot map (migrate/labels.go);\n- it refuses as soon as refs/work-issues/* holds anything, so it only works on a fresh store.\n\nThe shape for a git-bug user:\n1. Read refs/bugs/* directly. The first namespace move (misc/migrate/bugs-to-issues.sh, deleted in 50f3b00c) was only a rename of the same objects, so no rename step is needed; the prefix is an argument, or both are probed.\n2. The label -\u003e field mapping comes from the user (a section of the schema file or a flag), and a label with no mapping lands in `labels` instead of being refused.\n3. Decide what \"already migrated\" means once the store can have native issues next to imported ones: refuse per issue id rather than on any issue at all.\n4. Identities copy from refs/identities/* as bf6f392 already does.\n\nWhat it needs kept: entities/bug (the op decoder), package migrate, commands/migrate.go and TestIdsMatchBug (entities/issue/compat_test.go), which is what guarantees ids survive. Not the bug subcache, commands/bug or termui: migrate reads the entities directly and takes only the write lock.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core","cli"],"parent":"6555e3625dd41c628ed31a5c3bc69454ce4f9e92a5196401e88baa9554db1810","priority":"lowest","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}